// bubbler profile: spotify
//
// Sound is `pulseaudio`: the client and its CEF layer carry
// libpulse.so.0 (/opt/spotify/spotify and /opt/spotify/libcef.so both
// name it) and reach the server through $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pulse/native,
// which is what that grant binds. `pipewire` binds only pipewire-0, the
// native socket, and is for a client that speaks PipeWire itself or for
// the screen-share portal. Either socket carries capture as well as
// playback: this is the microphone too.
//
// No `talk "org.freedesktop.secrets"`: a music player's session token is
// adequately kept in its own config file in the private home, and the
// rule would let it talk to whatever process holds every password you
// have.
//
// `network` is the sandbox's own network namespace, so Spotify Connect
// finds no devices: discovery is mDNS on the LAN and pasta does not
// bridge. `network "host"` restores it at the price of the host's own
// loopback services.
//
// `wayland` is the display, and the only one: the sandbox has no X
// display at all, so the client's Chromium layer takes the socket that
// grant binds.
//
// `dri` is the GPU: the client's Chromium layer initialises a GPU
// process on it — the shader caches it leaves in the private home are
// the evidence — and composites in software without it. Bare, so the
// sandbox gets the render nodes and not the card nodes: no EDID, no
// framebuffer geometry, no other client's buffers.
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dbus {
//       talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
//       talk "org.gnome.SettingsDaemon.MediaKeys"
//   }
//     — the power-save blocker CEF holds during playback, and GNOME's
//       media-key grab, which the client asks for by that name. Both
//       strings are in /opt/spotify/libcef.so; on any other desktop
//       nothing owns the second and the rule is inert. CEF also tries
//       `org.freedesktop.PowerManagement`, so add that too if the screen
//       blanks during playback.
//   mpris name="spotify"
//     — media keys and the desktop's player controls. The exact name,
//       not a prefix: the app's own id is com.spotify.Client but the
//       player name it publishes is org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.spotify, and
//       a `*` here would own every player on the bus. Needs `dbus`.
//   notify
//     — the "now playing" notifications. Needs `dbus`.
//   tray
//     — the tray icon, which is libayatana-appindicator registering with
//       StatusNotifierWatcher. One rule, and the item itself is served on
//       the app's own unique name, so nothing needs `own`. Needs `dbus`.
//   portals
//     — a file chooser Spotify barely has; add it with
//       `home-share "Music"` if you play local files. Needs `dbus`.
wayland
dri
pulseaudio
network
command "spotify"
